Please note Known Risks have been assessed as part of this procurement and in accordance with the Procurement Act 2023, the Council reserves the right to modify this contract where such changes meet the criteria for permitted modifications under Section 74 and Schedule 8 of the Act. This includes but is not limited to: 
> changes regarding any relevant Statutory, Regulatory, Case Law and Government Legislation changes;
> changes to industry requirements relating to electrical safety and compliance;
> the right to decrease/increase the value of the Contract due changes in annual budget setting;
> changes to housing stock numbers, property types or geographical areas served;
> identification of previously unknown defects, compliance failures or asset condition issues;
> the implementation of retrofit decarbonisation or energy efficiency programmes;
> receipt of external funding or investment leading to increased work volumes;
> emergency response requirements arising from major incidents or unforeseen events;
> supply chain disruption, product shortages or manufacturer discontinuations;
> changes to product standards, technical specifications or approved products; and
> changes to service delivery, storage, logistics or distribution requirements.
Any such modifications shall be undertaken in compliance with the permitted grounds set out in Section 74 and Schedule 8 of the Act, including but not limited to modifications arising from unforeseeable circumstances or the materialisation of a known risk.

tender.description:
The purpose of the work is to identify, test and refine a movement
and public realm strategy. This Strategy must demonstrably achieve the following outcomes:
• Rebalance street space so the Town Centre functions primarily as a place for people rather than a
traffic corridor, by reducing excessive carriageway provision and re-purposing this space as a
high-quality public realm and placemaking opportunity that positively connects the shop parade,
allocated development sites and Hillingdon Underground Station;
• Improve the pedestrian and cycling infrastructure, delivering safer, more accessible, legible and
attractive routes within and through the Town Centre;
• Positively integrate the bus station identifying the optimal location to make this a high quality bus
interchange to include the Oxford Tube services, as a core component of the public realm;
• Identify safe, legible and deliverable access arrangements to the SHLAA site to the north of the junction, fully integrated with the wider movement network and public realm; 
• Improves the Hillingdon Underground Station approach giving consideration to car park capacity, taxi provision and EV infrastructure; 
• Accommodates movement infrastructure that connects through the Master Brewer site to and from the proposed Wealdstone Football Club development (5,900-10,000 capacity stadium) from the Hillingdon Underground Station and setting out additional facilities required for the stadium that would impact land take;
 • Test the potential to remove the A40 slip road at the Hillingdon Town Centre, taking account of the proximity of alternative slip road provision to the west and wider network performance.

Cambridge Folk Festival seeks experienced suppliers to submit a quotation for:
•	the provision of power, lighting & sound for the 2027 Folk Festival, dates of which are Friday 30 July, Saturday 31 July and Sunday 1 August 2027;
•	the provision of power, lighting & sound for the 2028 Folk Festival, dates to be confirmed but expected to be similar if the event goes ahead;
We are looking to award the contract for the 2027 Folk Festival with 1 x optional extension to cover year 2028. 
Please note we would like to receive prices for each year separately but please note year 2028 is not guaranteed. The contract will include optional extensions, please ensure you price accordingly.
Full details of the services required, including specific requirements, and any additional obligations, are set out in the specification documents. Suppliers are expected to review these carefully when preparing their quotation.
